answers.workaround:
In theory it could be worked around like this:
```
var _object_to_spawn: PackedScene
@export var object_to_spawn: PackedScene:
	get = get_my_prop, set = set_my_prop

func get_my_prop():
	return _object_to_spawn

func set_my_prop(value : PackedScene):
	var node_type : String = value.get_state().get_node_type(0)
	if(node_type == "Bullet"):
		_object_to_spawn = value
	else:
		print("Use PackedScene of type <Bullet>")
		_object_to_spawn = null
```
but this would cause the assignment to simply vanish if the wrong value is selected + it would still not filter the value which can be selected.
